# File: tests/blender/test_material_variants.py, tests/unit/test_material_variants_host.py
# Generated from: specs/148-let-one-finalized-asset-declare-several-material-variants/requirements.md
Feature: Material variants for finalized assets

  @SCN001
  Scenario: An asset declares its material variants
    Given Crate.material-variants.json beside the .blend declares Red with a base-colour texture and Blue with a Tint on M_Crate_Body
    When the validate step runs
    Then finalize uses that declaration
    And the validate report lists Red and Blue with their material and texture or parameters

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A texture-based material variant reaches Desktop and Mobile
    Given Crate declares Red on M_Crate_Body with a replacement base-colour texture
    When finalize all runs
    Then each export folder holds T_Crate_Body_BC_Red.png at that folder's T_Crate_Body_BC size
    And import_ue creates MI_Crate_Body_Red in each Content folder with BaseColor from the Red texture and Normal and ORM from the main set

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A parameter-based material variant uses Tint
    Given Crate declares Blue on M_Crate_Body with a Tint value and no texture
    When finalize all runs
    Then import_ue creates MI_Crate_Body_Blue in each Content folder with the main textures and the declared Tint
    And no Blue texture is exported or imported
    And M_NmgORM multiplies base colour by Tint, which defaults to white

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The main asset is unchanged
    Given an asset with material variants and an asset without a declaration
    When finalize all runs
    Then mesh slots stay bound to the main MI_<Name>_<Part>
    And the asset without a declaration produces the same exports, sidecar, and bindings as before

  @SCN005
  Scenario: The contract rejects an invalid declaration
    Given a declaration that breaks one material_variant rule
    When validate runs
    Then it fails with that material_variant finding naming the asset and the material variant
    And nothing is baked, exported, or imported

  @SCN006
  Scenario: A material variant on a merged material is rejected
    Given an asset whose bake merges its authored materials into M_<Name>_Body
    When it declares a material variant on one of the merged authored materials
    Then validate fails with material_variant.material_merged naming M_<Name>_Body

  @SCN007
  Scenario: The sidecar and import result record material variants
    Given finalize ran on an asset with material variants
    When the run finishes
    Then nmg-variants.json lists each material variant for desktop and mobile with its material, texture or parameters, and instance name
    And the import_ue result lists the variant textures and material instance paths

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Material variants are listed from Unreal
    Given Crate was finalized with material variants Red and Blue
    When the caller runs list_material_variants for Crate
    Then it returns Red and Blue with their material slot and Desktop and Mobile instance paths
    And an asset without material variants returns an empty list

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Removing a material variant deletes its stale assets
    Given Crate was finalized with Red and Blue
    When Blue is removed from the declaration and finalize all runs again
    Then Red is reused without duplicates
    And Blue's material instance and texture are deleted from Content and listed as removed
    And no Blue texture remains in the export folders

  @SCN010
  Scenario: The contract and skills document material variants
    Given the feature is merged
    When a contributor reads the asset contract, the finalize skill, and the finalize MCP reference
    Then they find the declaration format and location, the T_ and MI_ naming, the validation rules, stale deletion, and listing
